## std/carmen.pengu — fixed-layout binary records: pack and unpack by formula.
##
## `carmen` is PenguScript's answer to Python's `struct`: a compact formula
## string describes the layout of a binary record (`>I4sH` = big-endian u32,
## four bytes, u16) and the module reads or writes it without a schema class,
## a code generator or a C dependency. Every protocol with fixed offsets —
## TCP frame headers, PNG chunks, ELF headers, ZIP central directories, glTF
## chunks — becomes one formula plus one call.
##
## The name is Latin for *song* / *ritual formula*: the formula string is the
## incantation that turns bytes into values and back.
##
## ## Quick start
## ```pengu
## import std.carmen
##
## weave main into int:
##     var header as result of string to carmen.CarmenError is
##         calling carmen.pack with ">I4sH",
##             [(calling carmen.unsigned with 1),
##              (calling carmen.text with "abcd"),
##              (calling carmen.unsigned with 2)]
##     if not header.is_ok:
##         var why as string is calling header.error.message
##         calling print with "cannot pack: {why}\n"
##         banish why
##         return 1
##     defer banish header.value
##     var back as result of list of carmen.CarmenValue to carmen.CarmenError is
##         calling carmen.unpack with ">I4sH", header.value
##     if not back.is_ok:
##         return 1
##     defer banish back.value
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Layers
## | Layer | API | Use it when |
## |---|---|---|
## | Formula | `seal`, `calcsize`, `pack`, `unpack`, `unpack_named`, `explain` | the layout is data, not a type |
## | Cursor | `CarmenReader`, `CarmenWriter` | the record is streamed, partial or variable-length |
## | Insight | `layout`, `explain` | a parser misbehaves and you need to see offsets |
##
## ## Formula grammar
## A formula is a strict superset of Python's `struct` format:
## ```
## format := prefix? item*
## item   := prefix | field
## prefix := '@' | '=' | '<' | '>' | '!'
## field  := named | plain
## named  := '{' identifier ':' count? code '}'
## plain  := count? code
## ```
## - `@` native order **and** native alignment (the default), `=` native order
##   with standard alignment, `<` little, `>`/`!` big. A prefix may appear
##   again mid-formula to switch order for the following fields.
## - Codes: `x c b B ? h H i I l L q Q n N e f d s p P` (Python) plus `z`
##   (NUL-padded text, count required), `v`/`V` (little-endian u16/u32).
## - `{name:spec}` names a field for `layout`, `unpack_named` and `explain`.
##   Because `{}` interpolates in PenguScript, write named formulas as raw
##   strings: `r"{width:I}{height:I}"`.
## - Repeats produce one value each: `4B` yields four `Unsigned` values, while
##   `4s` yields one four-byte `Text`. A named repeat yields `flags`, `flags#1`,
##   `flags#2`, … so no value is lost.
##
## ## Python compatibility
## For every formula that uses only Python codes and prefixes, `carmen`
## produces byte-identical output to CPython's `struct` on the same platform,
## including native `long`/pointer sizes, alignment rules, `s`/`p` truncation,
## zero counts and out-of-range errors. Divergences are deliberate and small:
## malformed input is a `CarmenError` value (Python raises), `n`/`N`/`P` are
## rejected outside native mode, and `v`/`V`/`z`/named fields are extensions.
##
## ## Ownership
## | Value | Owns | Release with |
## |---|---|---|
## | `string` from `pack` / `explain` | its bytes | `banish` |
## | `list of CarmenValue` from `unpack` | the list and every `Text` | `banish` |
## | `Carmen` from `seal` | formula and field list | `banish` |
## | `CarmenReader` | nothing (borrows the data) | nothing |
## | `CarmenWriter` | its growing buffer | `banish` |
##
## A `CarmenReader` must not outlive the `string` it reads, and `view`/`sub`
## results must not outlive either.
##
## ## Complexity
## | Operation | Cost |
## |---|---|
## | `seal`, `calcsize`, `layout` | O(len formula) |
## | `pack` | O(len formula + size) |
## | `unpack` | O(len formula + values) |
## | `reader.read_*` | O(1) plus one result box |
## | `writer.write_*` | O(1) amortised |
## | `explain` | O(size) |
##
## ## Error table
## | Variant | Meaning |
## |---|---|
## | `BadFormat` | malformed formula (missing count, bad name, …) |
## | `UnknownCode` | a code that is not in the grammar |
## | `Truncated` | the buffer is shorter than the formula needs |
## | `TrailingBytes` | `unpack` received more bytes than the formula uses |
## | `ValueCountMismatch` | `pack` got the wrong number of values |
## | `ValueKindMismatch` | a value has the wrong variant for its field |
## | `ValueOutOfRange` | a value does not fit the field's width |
## | `UnnamedField` | a name was attached to a padding field |
## | `DuplicateName` | the same field name appears twice |
## | `BufferTooSmall` | `pack_into` target has no room |
## | `OffsetOutOfRange` | `unpack_from` offset is outside the buffer |
## | `MissingTerminator` | `read_cstr` found no NUL before the end |
## | `Unaligned` | a byte read started mid-byte in the bit cursor |

import std.ffi
import std.memoria
import std.builder

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module version
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Carmen module version.
const CARMEN_VERSION as string is "1.0.0"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C boundary: allocator, native sizes, byte copies
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Allocates `n` zeroed bytes as a raw owned `string`.
##
## ## Memory
## One allocation; release with `banish`.
antiquus _carmen_alloc with n as int into string:
    r"""
size_t bytes = (n > 0) ? (size_t)n : (size_t)0;
char *buf = (char *)calloc(bytes + 1, 1);
if (!buf) abort();
PenguString s;
s.data = buf;
s.len = (int)bytes;
s.is_owned = PENGU_STRING_OWNED_RAW;
return s;
"""

## Writable pointer to a raw byte buffer.
##
## ## Memory
## Borrows; no allocation.
antiquus _carmen_ptr with data as ref to string into ref to byte:
    r"""
return (uint8_t *)data->data;
"""

## Owned copy of `n` bytes starting at `off`.
##
## ## Memory
## One allocation; release with `banish`.
antiquus _carmen_copy_range with data as string, off as int, n as int into string:
    r"""
if (n <= 0 || !data.data || off < 0 || off > data.len || n > data.len - off)
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
return pengu_string_owned(data.data + off, n);
"""

## Borrowed `slice of byte` over `n` bytes at `off`.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; the slice aliases `data`.
antiquus _carmen_view with data as string, off as int, n as int into slice of byte:
    r"""
if (!data.data || off < 0 || off > data.len || n < 0 || n > data.len - off)
    return pengu_slice_new("", 1, 0);
return pengu_slice_new(data.data + off, 1, n);
"""

## `sizeof(long)` of the C compiler that will run the program.
antiquus _carmen_long_size into int:
    r"""
return (int)sizeof(long);
"""

## `_Alignof(long)` of the C compiler that will run the program.
antiquus _carmen_long_align into int:
    r"""
return (int)_Alignof(long);
"""

## `sizeof(void *)` of the target platform.
antiquus _carmen_ptr_size into int:
    r"""
return (int)sizeof(void *);
"""

## `_Alignof(void *)` of the target platform.
antiquus _carmen_ptr_align into int:
    r"""
return (int)_Alignof(void *);
"""

## Appends `n` bytes at `off` of `src` to a writer buffer, growing it.
##
## ## Memory
## May `realloc`; aborts on OOM like `std.builder`.
antiquus _carmen_reserve with data as ref to string, len as int, cap as ref to int, need as int into void:
    r"""
if (need <= *cap) return;
size_t want = (need > 16) ? (size_t)need : (size_t)16;
size_t ncap = (*cap > 0) ? (size_t)*cap : (size_t)16;
while (ncap < want) ncap *= 2;
char *np = (char *)realloc(data->data, ncap + 1);
if (!np) abort();
data->data = np;
data->len = (int)ncap;
data->is_owned = PENGU_STRING_OWNED_RAW;
*cap = (int)ncap;
"""

## Returns the writer buffer as an owned `string` of `len` bytes.
##
## ## Memory
## Transfers the buffer; the writer fields must be reset by the caller.
antiquus _carmen_take with data as ref to string, len as int into string:
    r"""
data->len = len;
return *data;
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte order
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Byte order of a field, a formula or a cursor.
##
## `Native` is only used while resolving prefixes; fields always store the
## resolved `Little` or `Big` order.
omen Endianness derive Nexus:
    ## Whatever the host CPU uses.
    Native
    ## Least significant byte first.
    Little
    ## Most significant byte first.
    Big

## Human name of an order.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling carmen.endian_name with carmen.Endianness.Big   # "big"
## ```
weave endian_name with e as Endianness into string:
    return judge (essence of (sigil of e)):
        when Native -> "native"
        when Little -> "little"
        when Big -> "big"

## Resolves the host byte order.
##
## ## Memory
## O(1); no allocation.
weave native_order into Endianness:
    var x as u16 is 1
    var p as ref to byte is transmute (sigil of x) to ref to byte
    if (p at 0) == 1:
        return Endianness.Little
    return Endianness.Big

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Values
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## One value read from, or written to, a binary record.
##
## A tagged union instead of a single `i64`: the wire distinguishes signed from
## unsigned and a `u32` field must not silently accept `-1`.
omen CarmenValue derive Nexus:
    ## A signed integer field (`b`, `h`, `i`, `l`, `q`, `n`).
    Signed with value as i64
    ## An unsigned integer field (`B`, `H`, `I`, `L`, `Q`, `N`, `P`, `v`, `V`).
    Unsigned with value as u64
    ## A floating point field (`e`, `f`, `d`).
    Real with value as f64
    ## A boolean field (`?`).
    Truth with value as bool
    ## A text field (`c`, `s`, `p`, `z`).
    Text with value as string

## Wraps a signed integer.
weave signed with v as i64 into CarmenValue:
    return with Signed is v

## Wraps an unsigned integer.
weave unsigned with v as u64 into CarmenValue:
    return with Unsigned is v

## Wraps a floating point number.
weave real with v as f64 into CarmenValue:
    return with Real is v

## Wraps a boolean.
weave truth with v as bool into CarmenValue:
    return with Truth is v

## Wraps a text value.
weave text with v as string into CarmenValue:
    return with Text is v

enchanting CarmenValue:
    ## True when the value is a signed integer.
    weave is_signed into bool:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when Signed -> true
            else -> false

    ## True when the value is an unsigned integer.
    weave is_unsigned into bool:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when Unsigned -> true
            else -> false

    ## True when the value is a float.
    weave is_real into bool:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when Real -> true
            else -> false

    ## True when the value is a boolean.
    weave is_truth into bool:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when Truth -> true
            else -> false

    ## True when the value is text.
    weave is_text into bool:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when Text -> true
            else -> false

    ## The signed payload, when the value is signed.
    weave as_signed into maybe i64:
        var out as maybe i64 is maybe none
        var ignored as int is judge (essence of self):
            when Signed with value ->
                set out is some value
                0
            else ->
                0
        return out

    ## The unsigned payload, when the value is unsigned.
    weave as_unsigned into maybe u64:
        var out as maybe u64 is maybe none
        var ignored as int is judge (essence of self):
            when Unsigned with value ->
                set out is some value
                0
            else ->
                0
        return out

    ## The float payload, when the value is real.
    weave as_real into maybe f64:
        var out as maybe f64 is maybe none
        var ignored as int is judge (essence of self):
            when Real with value ->
                set out is some value
                0
            else ->
                0
        return out

    ## The boolean payload, when the value is a truth value.
    weave as_truth into maybe bool:
        var out as maybe bool is maybe none
        var ignored as int is judge (essence of self):
            when Truth with value ->
                set out is some value
                0
            else ->
                0
        return out

    ## The text payload, when the value is text.
    weave as_text into maybe string:
        var out as maybe string is maybe none
        var ignored as int is judge (essence of self):
            when Text with value ->
                set out is some (calling _carmen_dup with value)
                0
            else ->
                0
        return out

    ## Name of the variant, for diagnostics.
    weave type_name into string:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when Signed -> "signed"
            when Unsigned -> "unsigned"
            when Real -> "real"
            when Truth -> "truth"
            when Text -> "text"

## Owned copy of a string.
##
## ## Memory
## One allocation; release with `banish`.
antiquus _carmen_dup with s as string into string:
    r"""
if (!s.data || s.len <= 0) return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
return pengu_string_owned(s.data, s.len);
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Errors
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Everything that can go wrong while reading, writing or compiling a formula.
##
## Malformed bytes are normal input here, so every failure is a value; `carmen`
## never panics on user data.
omen CarmenError derive Nexus:
    ## The formula is malformed.
    BadFormat with reason as string, position as int
    ## The formula contains a character that is not a code.
    UnknownCode with code as char, position as int
    ## The buffer is shorter than the formula needs.
    Truncated with need as int, have as int
    ## `unpack` received more bytes than the formula consumes.
    TrailingBytes with extra as int
    ## `pack` received the wrong number of values.
    ValueCountMismatch with expected as int, got as int
    ## A value's variant does not match its field.
    ValueKindMismatch with index as int, expected as string
    ## A value does not fit the field's width.
    ValueOutOfRange with index as int, detail as string
    ## A name was attached to a field that produces no value.
    UnnamedField with position as int
    ## The same field name appears twice.
    DuplicateName with name as string
    ## A `pack_into` target is too small.
    BufferTooSmall with need as int, capacity as int
    ## An `unpack_from` offset is outside the buffer.
    OffsetOutOfRange with offset as int, length as int
    ## `read_cstr` reached the end without a NUL byte.
    MissingTerminator with position as int
    ## A byte-sized read started in the middle of a byte.
    Unaligned with position as int

enchanting CarmenError:
    ## One English sentence describing the failure.
    weave message into string:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when BadFormat with reason, position ->
                "format: {reason} at position {position}"
            when UnknownCode with code, position ->
                "format: unknown code {ord code} at position {position}"
            when Truncated with need, have ->
                "buffer: need {need} bytes, have {have}"
            when TrailingBytes with extra ->
                "buffer: {extra} trailing bytes"
            when ValueCountMismatch with expected, got ->
                "values: need {expected}, got {got}"
            when ValueKindMismatch with index, expected ->
                "value {index}: expected {expected}"
            when ValueOutOfRange with index, detail ->
                "value {index}: {detail}"
            when UnnamedField with position ->
                "format: a padding field cannot be named (position {position})"
            when DuplicateName with name ->
                "format: duplicate field name '{name}'"
            when BufferTooSmall with need, capacity ->
                "buffer: need {need} bytes, capacity {capacity}"
            when OffsetOutOfRange with offset, length ->
                "buffer: offset {offset} is outside 0..{length}"
            when MissingTerminator with position ->
                "text: no NUL terminator before position {position}"
            when Unaligned with position ->
                "bit cursor: byte read at bit offset {position}"

## True when the formula uses only Python codes and prefixes.
##
## ## Memory
## O(len formula).
weave is_python_compatible with fmt as string into bool:
    var i as int is 0
    var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of fmt
    while i < fmt.length:
        var c as char is (bb at i) to char
        if c == 'z' or c == 'v' or c == 'V' or c == '{' or c == '}':
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Character classes
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

weave _is_space with c as char into bool:
    var v as int is ord c
    return v == 32 or v == 9 or v == 10 or v == 13

weave _is_digit with c as char into bool:
    var v as int is ord c
    return v >= 48 and v <= 57

weave _is_ident_start with c as char into bool:
    var v as int is ord c
    return (v >= 65 and v <= 90) or (v >= 97 and v <= 122) or v == 95

weave _is_ident_char with c as char into bool:
    var v as int is ord c
    return (v >= 65 and v <= 90) or (v >= 97 and v <= 122) or (v >= 48 and v <= 57) or v == 95

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code classification
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## True when `c` is a formula code.
weave _is_code with c as char into bool:
    if c == 'x' or c == 'c' or c == 'b' or c == 'B' or c == '?':
        return true
    if c == 'h' or c == 'H' or c == 'i' or c == 'I':
        return true
    if c == 'l' or c == 'L' or c == 'q' or c == 'Q':
        return true
    if c == 'n' or c == 'N' or c == 'e' or c == 'f' or c == 'd':
        return true
    if c == 's' or c == 'p' or c == 'P' or c == 'z':
        return true
    if c == 'v' or c == 'V':
        return true
    return false

## 0 = padding, 1 = signed, 2 = unsigned, 3 = float, 4 = text, 5 = char, 6 = bool.
weave _code_class with c as char into int:
    if c == 'x':
        return 0
    if c == 'b' or c == 'h' or c == 'i' or c == 'l' or c == 'q' or c == 'n':
        return 1
    if c == 'B' or c == 'H' or c == 'I' or c == 'L' or c == 'Q' or c == 'N' or c == 'P':
        return 2
    if c == 'v':
        return 2
    if c == 'V':
        return 2
    if c == 'e' or c == 'f' or c == 'd':
        return 3
    if c == 's' or c == 'p' or c == 'z':
        return 4
    if c == 'c':
        return 5
    if c == '?':
        return 6
    return -1

## Size in bytes of one element of `c`; 1 for text/padding (the count is the size).
weave _elem_size with c as char, native as bool into int:
    if c == 'b' or c == 'B' or c == 'c' or c == '?' or c == 'x':
        return 1
    if c == 'h' or c == 'H' or c == 'v' or c == 'e':
        return 2
    if c == 'i' or c == 'I' or c == 'V' or c == 'f':
        return 4
    if c == 'q' or c == 'Q' or c == 'd':
        return 8
    if c == 'l' or c == 'L':
        if native:
            return calling _carmen_long_size
        return 4
    if c == 'n' or c == 'N' or c == 'P':
        if native:
            return calling _carmen_ptr_size
        return 0
    if c == 's' or c == 'p' or c == 'z':
        return 1
    return 0

## Native alignment of one element of `c`.
weave _elem_align with c as char into int:
    if c == 'l' or c == 'L':
        return calling _carmen_long_align
    if c == 'n' or c == 'N' or c == 'P':
        return calling _carmen_ptr_align
    return calling _elem_size with c, true

## Rounds `off` up to the next multiple of `a`.
weave _align_up with off as int, a as int into int:
    if a <= 1:
        return off
    var r as int is off - ((off / a) * a)
    if r == 0:
        return off
    return off + (a - r)

## True when `c` may only be used in native mode.
weave _native_only with c as char into bool:
    return c == 'n' or c == 'N' or c == 'P'

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error constructors (keep call sites short)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

weave _bad with reason as string, position as int into CarmenError:
    return with BadFormat is with reason is reason, position is position

weave _unknown with code as char, position as int into CarmenError:
    return with UnknownCode is with code is code, position is position

weave _truncated with need as int, have as int into CarmenError:
    return with Truncated is with need is need, have is have

weave _count_mismatch with expected as int, got as int into CarmenError:
    return with ValueCountMismatch is with expected is expected, got is got

weave _kind_mismatch with index as int, expected as string into CarmenError:
    return with ValueKindMismatch is with index is index, expected is expected

weave _out_of_range with index as int, detail as string into CarmenError:
    return with ValueOutOfRange is with index is index, detail is detail

weave _duplicate with name as string into CarmenError:
    return with DuplicateName is with name is name

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fields and compiled formulas
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## One element of a compiled formula.
rune CarmenField derive Nexus:
    ## Field name from `{name:spec}`, or `""` when unnamed.
    name as string
    ## Formula code (`I`, `4s`, `x`, …).
    code as char
    ## Byte offset from the start of the record.
    offset as int
    ## Size in bytes (`4s` is 4, `B` is 1, `3x` is 3).
    size as int
    ## Alignment in bytes (1 in standard mode).
    alignment as int
    ## Value slot (0, 1, …), or `-1` for padding.
    index as int
    ## Byte order in force for this field.
    order as Endianness

## A compiled formula. Compile once, reuse for many records.
rune Carmen derive Nexus:
    _fmt as string
    _fields as list of CarmenField
    _size as int
    _order as Endianness
    _native as bool

enchanting Carmen:
    ## Total record size in bytes.
    weave size into int:
        return self->_size

    ## Formula string this handle was compiled from.
    weave format into string:
        return self->_fmt

    ## Default byte order.
    weave order into Endianness:
        return self->_order

    ## True when the formula starts in native mode.
    weave is_native into bool:
        return self->_native

    ## Number of values the formula consumes.
    weave value_count into int:
        var k as int is 0
        for f in self->_fields:
            if f.index >= 0:
                set k is k + 1
        return k

    ## Copies every field, duplicating names.
    weave fields into list of CarmenField:
        var out as list of CarmenField is list of CarmenField
        for f in self->_fields:
            var nm as string is ""
            if f.name != "":
                set nm is calling _carmen_dup with f.name
            var g as CarmenField is with name is nm, code is f.code, offset is f.offset, size is f.size, alignment is f.alignment, index is f.index, order is f.order
            calling out.push with g
        return out

## Compiles `fmt` into a reusable handle.
##
## ## Example
## `let h is calling carmen.seal with ">I4sH"`
##
## ## Complexity
## O(len fmt).
weave seal with fmt as string into result of Carmen to CarmenError:
    var fields as list of CarmenField is list of CarmenField
    var off as int is 0
    var order as Endianness is Native
    var native as bool is true
    var vcount as int is 0
    var first_order as Endianness is Native
    var first_native as bool is true
    var saw_prefix as bool is false
    var i as int is 0
    var n as int is fmt.length
    var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of fmt
    while i < n:
        var c as char is (bb at i) to char
        if calling _is_space with c:
            set i is i + 1
            continue
        if c == '@' or c == '=' or c == '<' or c == '>' or c == '!':
            if c == '@':
                set native is true
                set order is Native
            else if c == '=':
                set native is false
                set order is Native
            else if c == '<':
                set native is false
                set order is Little
            else:
                set native is false
                set order is Big
            if not saw_prefix:
                set saw_prefix is true
                set first_order is order
                if c == '@':
                    set first_native is true
                else:
                    set first_native is false
            set i is i + 1
            continue
        var iname as string is ""
        var named as bool is false
        if c == '{':
            set named is true
            set i is i + 1
            var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
            var closed as bool is false
            while i < n:
                var cc as char is (bb at i) to char
                if cc == ':':
                    set closed is true
                    set i is i + 1
                    break
                calling sb.append_char with cc
                set i is i + 1
            if not closed:
                banish sb
                return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "named field has no ':'", i)
            set iname is calling sb.finish
            banish sb
            if iname.length == 0:
                return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "empty field name", i)
            var q as int is 0
            var nb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of iname
            while q < iname.length:
                var qc as char is (nb at q) to char
                var ok as bool is false
                if q == 0:
                    set ok is calling _is_ident_start with qc
                else:
                    set ok is calling _is_ident_char with qc
                if not ok:
                    banish iname
                    return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "field name must be an identifier", i)
                set q is q + 1
        var count as int is 0
        var has_count as bool is false
        while i < n:
            var d as char is (bb at i) to char
            if not calling _is_digit with d:
                break
            if count > 100000000:
                if iname != "":
                    banish iname
                return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "count is too large", i)
            set count is (count * 10) + ((ord d) - 48)
            set has_count is true
            set i is i + 1
        if i >= n:
            if iname != "":
                banish iname
            return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "formula ends after a count", i)
        var code as char is (bb at i) to char
        var code_pos as int is i
        set i is i + 1
        if not calling _is_code with code:
            if iname != "":
                banish iname
            return calling err_of with (calling _unknown with code, code_pos)
        if named:
            if code == 'x':
                banish iname
                return calling err_of with (with UnnamedField is with position is code_pos)
            if i >= n or ((bb at i) to char) != '}':
                banish iname
                return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "named field is missing '}'", i)
            set i is i + 1
            var dup as bool is false
            for f in fields:
                if f.name == iname:
                    set dup is true
            if dup:
                banish iname
                return calling err_of with (calling _duplicate with iname)
        if code == 'x':
            var padn as int is 1
            if has_count:
                set padn is count
            if padn > 0:
                var pf as CarmenField is with name is "", code is code, offset is off, size is padn, alignment is 1, index is -1, order is order
                calling fields.push with pf
                set off is off + padn
            if iname != "":
                banish iname
            continue
        if code == 's' or code == 'p' or code == 'z':
            var tn as int is 1
            if has_count:
                set tn is count
            if code == 'z' and not has_count:
                if iname != "":
                    banish iname
                return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "code 'z' requires a count", code_pos)
            if code == 'p' and tn > 255:
                if iname != "":
                    banish iname
                return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "code 'p' allows at most 255 bytes", code_pos)
            var tf as CarmenField is with name is iname, code is code, offset is off, size is tn, alignment is 1, index is vcount, order is order
            calling fields.push with tf
            set vcount is vcount + 1
            set off is off + tn
            continue
        if calling _native_only with code and not native:
            if iname != "":
                banish iname
            return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "codes 'n', 'N' and 'P' are native-only", code_pos)
        var elem as int is calling _elem_size with code, native
        var al as int is calling _elem_align with code
        if has_count and count == 0:
            if native:
                set off is calling _align_up with off, al
            if iname != "":
                banish iname
            continue
        var reps as int is 1
        if has_count:
            set reps is count
        var r as int is 0
        while r < reps:
            if native:
                set off is calling _align_up with off, al
            var nm as string is ""
            if iname != "":
                if r == 0:
                    set nm is iname
                else:
                    set nm is "{iname}#{r}"
            var f as CarmenField is with name is nm, code is code, offset is off, size is elem, alignment is al, index is vcount, order is order
            calling fields.push with f
            set vcount is vcount + 1
            set off is off + elem
            set r is r + 1
        if iname != "" and reps == 0:
            banish iname
    var handle as Carmen is with _fmt is (calling _carmen_dup with fmt), _fields is fields, _size is off, _order is first_order, _native is first_native
    return calling ok_of with handle

## Size in bytes of the record described by `fmt`.
##
## ## Example
## `let n is calling carmen.calcsize with ">I4sH"` → `10`
weave calcsize with fmt as string into result of int to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var sz as int is calling h.size
    banish h
    return calling ok_of with sz

## Fields of `fmt`, with offsets, sizes and alignments.
##
## ## Example
## `let fs is calling carmen.layout with "<2sI"` → two fields at offsets 0 and 2
weave layout with fmt as string into result of list of CarmenField to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var fs as list of CarmenField is calling h.fields
    banish h
    return calling ok_of with fs

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte order
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## True when `e` means little-endian on this platform.
weave _is_little with e as Endianness into bool:
    return judge (essence of (sigil of e)):
        when Native -> calling _native_is_little
        when Little -> true
        when Big -> false

antiquus _native_is_little into bool:
    r"""
uint16_t probe = 1;
return *(uint8_t *)&probe == 1;
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw integer and float access
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Reads `n` bytes at `off` as an unsigned integer.
weave _get_u with data as string, off as int, n as int, e as Endianness into u64:
    var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of data
    var v as u64 is 0
    var k as int is 0
    var little as bool is calling _is_little with e
    while k < n:
        var b as u64 is (bb at (off + k)) to u64
        if little:
            set v is v | (b << (k * 8))
        else:
            set v is (v << 8) | b
        set k is k + 1
    return v

## Writes the low `n` bytes of `v` at `off`.
weave _put_u with data as ref to string, off as int, n as int, v as u64, e as Endianness into void:
    var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with data
    var k as int is 0
    var little as bool is calling _is_little with e
    while k < n:
        var shift as int is (n - 1 - k) * 8
        if little:
            set shift is k * 8
        var b as byte is ((v >> shift) & 255) to byte
        set p at (off + k) is b
        set k is k + 1

antiquus _f32_from_bits with b as u32 into float:
    r"""
union { uint32_t u; float f; } x;
x.u = b;
return x.f;
"""

antiquus _f32_bits with f as float into u32:
    r"""
union { uint32_t u; float f; } x;
x.f = f;
return x.u;
"""

antiquus _f64_from_bits with b as u64 into f64:
    r"""
union { uint64_t u; double f; } x;
x.u = b;
return x.f;
"""

antiquus _f64_bits with f as f64 into u64:
    r"""
union { uint64_t u; double f; } x;
x.f = f;
return x.u;
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IEEE 754 binary16
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Converts a half-precision bit pattern to a 32-bit float.
weave _half_to_f32 with h as u16 into float:
    var sign as u32 is ((h to u32) >> 15) & 1
    var exp as u32 is ((h to u32) >> 10) & 31
    var mant as u32 is (h to u32) & 1023
    var bits as u32 is 0
    if exp == 0:
        if mant == 0:
            set bits is sign << 31
        else:
            var e as int is -1
            var m as u32 is mant
            while (m & 1024) == 0:
                set m is m << 1
                set e is e + 1
            set m is m & 1023
            set bits is (sign << 31) | ((112 - (e to u32)) << 23) | (m << 13)
    else if exp == 31:
        set bits is (sign << 31) | 2139095040 | (mant << 13)
    else:
        set bits is (sign << 31) | ((exp + 112) << 23) | (mant << 13)
    return calling _f32_from_bits with bits

## Converts a 32-bit float to a half-precision bit pattern.
##
## ## Errors
## Finite values outside ±65504 produce `ValueOutOfRange`.
weave _f32_to_half with f as float, idx as int into result of u16 to CarmenError:
    var bits as u32 is calling _f32_bits with f
    var sign as u32 is (bits >> 31) & 1
    var exp as u32 is (bits >> 23) & 255
    var mant as u32 is bits & 8388607
    if exp == 255:
        if mant == 0:
            return calling ok_of with (((sign << 15) | 31744) to u16)
        return calling ok_of with (((sign << 15) | 31744 | (mant >> 13)) to u16)
    if exp == 0 and mant == 0:
        return calling ok_of with ((sign << 15) to u16)
    var e as int is (exp to int) - 127
    if e > 15:
        return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "float too large for a half field")
    if e >= -14:
        var m as u32 is mant >> 13
        var rem as u32 is mant & 8191
        if rem > 4096 or (rem == 4096 and (m & 1) == 1):
            set m is m + 1
            if m == 1024:
                set m is 0
                set e is e + 1
                if e > 15:
                    return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "float too large for a half field")
        return calling ok_of with (((sign << 15) | (((e + 15) to u32) << 10) | m) to u16)
    if e < -25:
        return calling ok_of with ((sign << 15) to u16)
    var shift as int is -14 - e
    var m2 as u32 is (mant | 8388608) >> (shift + 13)
    var rem2 as u32 is (mant | 8388608) & ((1 << (shift + 13)) - 1)
    var halfway as u32 is 1 << (shift + 12)
    if rem2 > halfway or (rem2 == halfway and (m2 & 1) == 1):
        set m2 is m2 + 1
    return calling ok_of with (((sign << 15) | m2) to u16)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Value coercion
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

weave _signed_max with size as int into i64:
    if size >= 8:
        return 9223372036854775807
    var m as i64 is 1
    return (m << ((size * 8) - 1)) - 1

weave _signed_min with size as int into i64:
    if size >= 8:
        return -9223372036854775807 - 1
    var m as i64 is 1
    return -(m << ((size * 8) - 1))

weave _unsigned_max with size as int into u64:
    if size >= 8:
        var all as u64 is 0
        return all - 1
    var m as u64 is 1
    return (m << (size * 8)) - 1

## Extracts an integer (any width) from a value.
weave _as_i64 with v as CarmenValue, idx as int into result of i64 to CarmenError:
    var outv as result of i64 to CarmenError is calling ok_of with (0 to i64)
    judge (essence of (sigil of v)):
        when Signed with value ->
            set outv is calling ok_of with value
        when Unsigned with value ->
            if value > 9223372036854775807:
                set outv is calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "integer does not fit a signed field")
            else:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (value to i64)
        when Truth with value ->
            if value:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (1 to i64)
            else:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (0 to i64)
        else ->
            set outv is calling err_of with (calling _kind_mismatch with idx, "an integer")
    return outv

weave _as_u64 with v as CarmenValue, idx as int into result of u64 to CarmenError:
    var outv as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling ok_of with (0 to u64)
    judge (essence of (sigil of v)):
        when Unsigned with value ->
            set outv is calling ok_of with value
        when Signed with value ->
            if value < 0:
                set outv is calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "negative integer in an unsigned field")
            else:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (value to u64)
        when Truth with value ->
            if value:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (1 to u64)
            else:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (0 to u64)
        else ->
            set outv is calling err_of with (calling _kind_mismatch with idx, "an integer")
    return outv

weave _as_f64 with v as CarmenValue, idx as int into result of f64 to CarmenError:
    var outv as result of f64 to CarmenError is calling ok_of with (0.0 to f64)
    judge (essence of (sigil of v)):
        when Real with value ->
            set outv is calling ok_of with value
        when Signed with value ->
            set outv is calling ok_of with (value to f64)
        when Unsigned with value ->
            set outv is calling ok_of with (value to f64)
        when Truth with value ->
            if value:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (1.0 to f64)
            else:
                set outv is calling ok_of with (0.0 to f64)
        else ->
            set outv is calling err_of with (calling _kind_mismatch with idx, "a number")
    return outv

weave _as_text with v as CarmenValue, idx as int into result of string to CarmenError:
    var outv as result of string to CarmenError is calling ok_of with ""
    judge (essence of (sigil of v)):
        when Text with value ->
            set outv is calling ok_of with value
        else ->
            set outv is calling err_of with (calling _kind_mismatch with idx, "text")
    return outv

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encoding
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Copies `src` into a byte buffer at `off`.
antiquus _copy_to with src as string, dst as ref to byte, off as int into void:
    r"""
if (!src.data || src.len <= 0) return;
memcpy(dst + off, src.data, (size_t)src.len);
"""

weave _pack_text with f as CarmenField, v as CarmenValue, out as ref to string, idx as int into result of void to CarmenError:
    var tx as result of string to CarmenError is calling _as_text with v, idx
    if not tx.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with tx.error
    var t as string is tx.value
    var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with out
    var tb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of t
    var n as int is f.size
    if f.code == 'p':
        if n > 0:
            var lim as int is n - 1
            var l as int is t.length
            if l > lim:
                set l is lim
            set p at (f.offset) is (l to byte)
            var k as int is 0
            while k < l:
                set p at ((f.offset + 1) + k) is (tb at k)
                set k is k + 1
            while k < lim:
                set p at ((f.offset + 1) + k) is 0
                set k is k + 1
        return calling ok_of with 0
    var l2 as int is t.length
    if l2 > n:
        set l2 is n
    var k2 as int is 0
    while k2 < l2:
        set p at (f.offset + k2) is (tb at k2)
        set k2 is k2 + 1
    while k2 < n:
        set p at (f.offset + k2) is 0
        set k2 is k2 + 1
    return calling ok_of with 0

weave _pack_field with f as CarmenField, v as CarmenValue, out as ref to string, idx as int into result of void to CarmenError:
    var cls as int is calling _code_class with f.code
    if cls == 0:
        return calling ok_of with 0
    if cls == 4:
        return calling _pack_text with f, v, out, idx
    if cls == 5:
        var tx as result of string to CarmenError is calling _as_text with v, idx
        if not tx.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with tx.error
        var t as string is tx.value
        if t.length != 1:
            return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "char field needs exactly one byte")
        var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with out
        var tb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of t
        set p at (f.offset) is (tb at 0)
        return calling ok_of with 0
    if cls == 6:
        var bv as bool is false
        var got as bool is false
        judge (essence of (sigil of v)):
            when Truth with value ->
                set bv is value
                set got is true
            when Signed with value ->
                set bv is value != 0
                set got is true
            when Unsigned with value ->
                set bv is value != 0
                set got is true
            else ->
                set got is false
        if not got:
            return calling err_of with (calling _kind_mismatch with idx, "truth")
        if bv:
            calling _put_u with out, f.offset, 1, 1, f.order
        else:
            calling _put_u with out, f.offset, 1, 0, f.order
        return calling ok_of with 0
    if cls == 3:
        var fx as result of f64 to CarmenError is calling _as_f64 with v, idx
        if not fx.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with fx.error
        var d as f64 is fx.value
        if f.code == 'd':
            calling _put_u with out, f.offset, 8, (calling _f64_bits with d), f.order
        else if f.code == 'f':
            if d > 3.4028234663852886e38 or d < -3.4028234663852886e38:
                return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "float too large for a single field")
            var f32 as float is d to float
            calling _put_u with out, f.offset, 4, (calling _f32_bits with f32) to u64, f.order
        else:
            var hx as result of u16 to CarmenError is calling _f32_to_half with (d to float), idx
            if not hx.is_ok:
                return calling err_of with hx.error
            calling _put_u with out, f.offset, 2, (hx.value to u64), f.order
        return calling ok_of with 0
    if cls == 1:
        var ix as result of i64 to CarmenError is calling _as_i64 with v, idx
        if not ix.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with ix.error
        var x as i64 is ix.value
        if x < calling _signed_min with f.size or x > calling _signed_max with f.size:
            return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "integer does not fit the field width")
        calling _put_u with out, f.offset, f.size, (x to u64), f.order
        return calling ok_of with 0
    var ux as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling _as_u64 with v, idx
    if not ux.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with ux.error
    var u as u64 is ux.value
    if u > calling _unsigned_max with f.size:
        return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with idx, "integer does not fit the field width")
    calling _put_u with out, f.offset, f.size, u, f.order
    return calling ok_of with 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decoding
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

weave _unpack_field with f as CarmenField, data as string into result of CarmenValue to CarmenError:
    var cls as int is calling _code_class with f.code
    var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of data
    if cls == 4:
        var n as int is f.size
        if f.code == 'p':
            if n <= 0:
                return calling ok_of with (with Text is "")
            var l as int is (bb at f.offset) to int
            if l > n - 1:
                set l is n - 1
            if l < 0:
                set l is 0
            return calling ok_of with (with Text is (calling _carmen_copy_range with data, f.offset + 1, l))
        if f.code == 'z':
            var k as int is 0
            while k < n:
                if ((bb at (f.offset + k)) to int) == 0:
                    break
                set k is k + 1
            return calling ok_of with (with Text is (calling _carmen_copy_range with data, f.offset, k))
        return calling ok_of with (with Text is (calling _carmen_copy_range with data, f.offset, n))
    if cls == 5:
        return calling ok_of with (with Text is (calling _carmen_copy_range with data, f.offset, 1))
    if cls == 6:
        var t as bool is ((bb at f.offset) to int) != 0
        return calling ok_of with (with Truth is t)
    if cls == 3:
        if f.code == 'd':
            var dv as f64 is calling _f64_from_bits with (calling _get_u with data, f.offset, 8, f.order)
            return calling ok_of with (with Real is dv)
        if f.code == 'f':
            var fv as float is calling _f32_from_bits with (calling _get_u with data, f.offset, 4, f.order) to u32
            return calling ok_of with (with Real is (fv to f64))
        var hv as float is calling _half_to_f32 with (calling _get_u with data, f.offset, 2, f.order) to u16
        return calling ok_of with (with Real is (hv to f64))
    if cls == 1:
        var raw as u64 is calling _get_u with data, f.offset, f.size, f.order
        var y as i64 is raw to i64
        if f.size < 8:
            var sh as int is 64 - (f.size * 8)
            set y is (y << sh) >> sh
        return calling ok_of with (with Signed is y)
    var ur as u64 is calling _get_u with data, f.offset, f.size, f.order
    return calling ok_of with (with Unsigned is ur)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Record decode/encode
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

antiquus _take_error_void with r as ref to result of void to CarmenError into CarmenError:
    r"""
CarmenError out;
memset(&out, 0, sizeof out);
if (!r || r->is_ok || !r->err_val) return out;
out = *(CarmenError *)r->err_val;
free(r->err_val);
r->err_val = NULL;
r->is_ok = true;
r->ok_val = NULL;
return out;
"""

antiquus _take_error_value with r as ref to result of CarmenValue to CarmenError into CarmenError:
    r"""
CarmenError out;
memset(&out, 0, sizeof out);
if (!r || r->is_ok || !r->err_val) return out;
out = *(CarmenError *)r->err_val;
free(r->err_val);
r->err_val = NULL;
r->is_ok = true;
r->ok_val = NULL;
return out;
"""

weave _decode_all with h as Carmen, data as string into result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError:
    var out as list of CarmenValue is list of CarmenValue
    for f in h._fields:
        if f.index >= 0:
            var r as result of CarmenValue to CarmenError is calling _unpack_field with f, data
            if not r.is_ok:
                var e as CarmenError is calling _take_error_value with (sigil of r)
                banish out
                return calling err_of with e
            calling out.push with r.value
    return calling ok_of with out

## Packs `values` into a new byte string using `fmt`.
##
## ## Example
## `calling carmen.pack with ">I4sH", [calling carmen.unsigned with 1, calling carmen.text with "abcd", calling carmen.unsigned with 2]`
##
## ## Errors
## `ValueCountMismatch`, `ValueKindMismatch`, `ValueOutOfRange`.
weave pack with fmt as string, values as list of CarmenValue into result of string to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var need as int is calling h.value_count
    var have as int is values.length
    var out as string is calling _carmen_alloc with (calling h.size)
    if have != need:
        banish out
        banish h
        return calling err_of with (calling _count_mismatch with need, have)
    var idx as int is 0
    for f in h._fields:
        if f.index >= 0:
            var r as result of void to CarmenError is calling _pack_field with f, (values at idx), (sigil of out), idx
            if not r.is_ok:
                var e as CarmenError is calling _take_error_void with (sigil of r)
                banish out
                banish h
                return calling err_of with e
            set idx is idx + 1
    banish h
    return calling ok_of with out

## Packs `values` into `buffer` at `offset`, returning the number of bytes
## written.
##
## ## Errors
## `BufferTooSmall` when `offset + size` exceeds `capacity`.
weave pack_into with fmt as string, buffer as ref to byte, capacity as int, offset as int, values as list of CarmenValue into result of int to CarmenError:
    var packed as result of string to CarmenError is calling pack with fmt, values
    if not packed.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with packed.error
    var blob as string is packed.value
    var end as int is offset + blob.length
    if offset < 0 or end > capacity:
        banish blob
        return calling err_of with (with BufferTooSmall is with need is end, capacity is capacity)
    calling _copy_to with blob, buffer, offset
    var n as int is blob.length
    banish blob
    return calling ok_of with n

## Unpacks exactly one record; the buffer must be exactly the record size.
##
## ## Errors
## `Truncated` or `TrailingBytes`.
weave unpack with fmt as string, data as string into result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var need as int is calling h.size
    if data.length < need:
        banish h
        return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with need, data.length)
    if data.length > need:
        banish h
        return calling err_of with (with TrailingBytes is with extra is (data.length - need))
    var out as result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError is calling _decode_all with h, data
    banish h
    return out

## Unpacks one record starting at `offset`; bytes after the record are ignored.
##
## ## Errors
## `OffsetOutOfRange` or `Truncated`.
weave unpack_from with fmt as string, data as string, offset as int into result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var need as int is calling h.size
    if offset < 0 or offset > data.length:
        banish h
        return calling err_of with (with OffsetOutOfRange is with offset is offset, length is data.length)
    var have as int is data.length - offset
    if have < need:
        banish h
        return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with need, have)
    var blob as string is calling _carmen_copy_range with data, offset, need
    var out as result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError is calling _decode_all with h, blob
    banish blob
    banish h
    return out

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Writer
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Grows a byte buffer and appends encoded values to it.
##
## The writer owns its buffer; `to_string` copies it, `take_string` transfers
## it.
rune CarmenWriter derive Nexus:
    _data as string
    _len as int
    _cap as int
    _order as Endianness
    _bit as int

## Creates an empty writer with a 256-byte buffer.
##
## ## Example
## `var w as carmen.CarmenWriter is calling carmen.new_writer`
weave new_writer into CarmenWriter:
    var buf as string is calling _carmen_alloc with 256
    return with _data is buf, _len is 0, _cap is 256, _order is Native, _bit is 0

## Creates an empty writer with at least `cap` bytes of buffer.
weave new_writer_with with cap as int into CarmenWriter:
    var n as int is 256
    if cap > 0:
        set n is cap
    var buf as string is calling _carmen_alloc with n
    return with _data is buf, _len is 0, _cap is n, _order is Native, _bit is 0

## Creates an empty writer that starts in `e`.
weave new_writer_endian with e as Endianness into CarmenWriter:
    var w as CarmenWriter is calling new_writer
    set w._order is e
    return w

enchanting CarmenWriter:
    ## Byte order used by the `write_*` methods.
    weave order into Endianness:
        return self->_order

    ## Selects the byte order for following writes.
    weave with_endian with e as Endianness into void:
        set self->_order is e

    ## Bytes appended so far.
    weave length into int:
        return self->_len

    ## Bytes of buffer currently reserved.
    weave capacity into int:
        return self->_cap

    weave _ensure with need as int into void:
        if need > self->_cap:
            calling _carmen_reserve with (sigil of self->_data), self->_len, (sigil of self->_cap), need

    ## Appends the raw bytes of `s`.
    weave write_raw with s as string into void:
        var need as int is self->_len + s.length
        calling self._ensure with need
        if s.length > 0:
            var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with (sigil of self->_data)
            calling _copy_to with s, p, self->_len
        set self->_len is need

    ## Appends a NUL-terminated copy of `s`.
    weave write_cstr with s as string into void:
        calling self.write_raw with s
        calling self.write_u8 with 0

    ## Appends `s` truncated or NUL-padded to exactly `n` bytes.
    weave write_fixed with s as string, n as int into void:
        if n <= 0:
            return
        calling self._ensure with (self->_len + n)
        var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with (sigil of self->_data)
        var sb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
        var l as int is s.length
        if l > n:
            set l is n
        var k as int is 0
        while k < l:
            set p at (self->_len + k) is (sb at k)
            set k is k + 1
        while k < n:
            set p at (self->_len + k) is 0
            set k is k + 1
        set self->_len is self->_len + n

    ## Appends `n` bits (1..64) MSB-first.
    ##
    ## Bits share a byte: after `write_bits 3, 5` the next `write_bits 5, 3`
    ## fills the same byte. Call `align_bits` before a byte-aligned write.
    weave write_bits with v as u64, n as int into void:
        if n <= 0 or n > 64:
            return
        var i as int is n - 1
        while i >= 0:
            if self->_bit == 0:
                calling self._ensure with (self->_len + 1)
                var pz as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with (sigil of self->_data)
                set pz at (self->_len) is 0
                set self->_len is self->_len + 1
            var bit as int is (((v >> (i to u64)) & 1) to int)
            var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with (sigil of self->_data)
            var cur as int is (p at (self->_len - 1)) to int
            if bit == 1:
                set cur is cur ^ (1 << (7 - self->_bit))
                set p at (self->_len - 1) is (cur to byte)
            set self->_bit is self->_bit + 1
            if self->_bit == 8:
                set self->_bit is 0
            set i is i - 1

    ## Pads the current partial bit byte so the next write starts aligned.
    weave align_bits into void:
        set self->_bit is 0

    ## Appends a Pascal string of exactly `n` bytes (length byte + text).
    weave write_pascal with s as string, n as int into void:
        if n <= 0:
            return
        var l as int is s.length
        if l > n - 1:
            set l is n - 1
        calling self._ensure with (self->_len + n)
        var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with (sigil of self->_data)
        set p at (self->_len) is (l to byte)
        var sb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
        var k as int is 0
        while k < l:
            set p at ((self->_len + 1) + k) is (sb at k)
            set k is k + 1
        while k < n - 1:
            set p at ((self->_len + 1) + k) is 0
            set k is k + 1
        set self->_len is self->_len + n

    ## Appends `n` zero bytes.
    weave pad with n as int into void:
        if n <= 0:
            return
        calling self._ensure with (self->_len + n)
        var p as ref to byte is calling _carmen_ptr with (sigil of self->_data)
        var k as int is 0
        while k < n:
            set p at (self->_len + k) is 0
            set k is k + 1
        set self->_len is self->_len + n

    ## Appends zero bytes until the length is a multiple of `a`.
    weave align with a as int into void:
        if a <= 1:
            return
        var r as int is self->_len - ((self->_len / a) * a)
        if r != 0:
            calling self.pad with (a - r)

    ## Appends a boolean as one byte.
    weave write_bool with v as bool into void:
        if v:
            calling self.write_u8 with 1
        else:
            calling self.write_u8 with 0

    ## Appends one character.
    weave write_char with c as char into void:
        calling self.write_u8 with (ord c)

    ## Appends an unsigned 8-bit integer.
    weave write_u8 with v as u64 into void:
        calling self._ensure with (self->_len + 1)
        calling _put_u with (sigil of self->_data), self->_len, 1, v, self->_order
        set self->_len is self->_len + 1

    ## Appends an unsigned 16-bit integer.
    weave write_u16 with v as u64 into void:
        calling self._ensure with (self->_len + 2)
        calling _put_u with (sigil of self->_data), self->_len, 2, v, self->_order
        set self->_len is self->_len + 2

    ## Appends an unsigned 32-bit integer.
    weave write_u32 with v as u64 into void:
        calling self._ensure with (self->_len + 4)
        calling _put_u with (sigil of self->_data), self->_len, 4, v, self->_order
        set self->_len is self->_len + 4

    ## Appends an unsigned 64-bit integer.
    weave write_u64 with v as u64 into void:
        calling self._ensure with (self->_len + 8)
        calling _put_u with (sigil of self->_data), self->_len, 8, v, self->_order
        set self->_len is self->_len + 8

    ## Appends a signed 8-bit integer.
    weave write_i8 with v as i64 into void:
        calling self.write_u8 with (v to u64)

    ## Appends a signed 16-bit integer.
    weave write_i16 with v as i64 into void:
        calling self.write_u16 with (v to u64)

    ## Appends a signed 32-bit integer.
    weave write_i32 with v as i64 into void:
        calling self.write_u32 with (v to u64)

    ## Appends a signed 64-bit integer.
    weave write_i64 with v as i64 into void:
        calling self.write_u64 with (v to u64)

    ## Appends a 32-bit float.
    weave write_f32 with v as float into void:
        calling self.write_u32 with (calling _f32_bits with v) to u64

    ## Appends a 64-bit float.
    weave write_f64 with v as f64 into void:
        calling self.write_u64 with (calling _f64_bits with v)

    ## Appends a half-precision float.
    ##
    ## ## Errors
    ## Finite values outside ±65504 produce `ValueOutOfRange`.
    weave write_f16 with v as f64 into result of void to CarmenError:
        var hx as result of u16 to CarmenError is calling _f32_to_half with (v to float), -1
        if not hx.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with hx.error
        calling self.write_u16 with (hx.value to u64)
        return calling ok_of with 0

    ## Appends an unsigned LEB128 varint.
    weave write_varint with v as u64 into void:
        var x as u64 is v
        while x >= 128:
            calling self.write_u8 with ((x & 127) | 128)
            set x is x >> 7
        calling self.write_u8 with x

    ## Appends a ZigZag + LEB128 signed varint.
    weave write_zigzag with v as i64 into void:
        var zz as u64 is (v to u64) << 1
        if v < 0:
            var all as u64 is 0
            set all is all - 1
            set zz is zz ^ all
        calling self.write_varint with zz

    ## Appends the record produced by `pack` for `fmt` and `values`.
    weave write_record with fmt as string, values as list of CarmenValue into result of void to CarmenError:
        var packed as result of string to CarmenError is calling pack with fmt, values
        if not packed.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with packed.error
        var blob as string is packed.value
        calling self.write_raw with blob
        banish blob
        return calling ok_of with 0

    ## Copies the buffer into a new owned string.
    weave to_string into string:
        return calling _carmen_copy_range with self->_data, 0, self->_len

    ## Transfers the buffer into an owned string and resets the writer.
    weave take_string into string:
        var out as string is calling _carmen_take with (sigil of self->_data), self->_len
        var fresh as string is calling _carmen_alloc with 16
        set self->_data is fresh
        set self->_len is 0
        set self->_cap is 16
        return out

    ## Discards every byte, keeping the buffer.
    weave clear into void:
        set self->_len is 0

    ## Grows the buffer to at least `n` bytes.
    weave reserve with n as int into void:
        calling self._ensure with n

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reader
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Reads values from an existing byte string with a moving cursor.
##
## The reader borrows its data; do not `banish` the source while a reader or a
## `view`/`sub` result is alive.
rune CarmenReader:
    _data as string
    _offset as int
    _end as int
    _bit as int
    _order as Endianness

## Creates a reader over `data` starting at byte 0.
##
## ## Example
## `var r as carmen.CarmenReader is calling carmen.new_reader with blob`
weave new_reader with data as string into CarmenReader:
    return with _data is data, _offset is 0, _end is data.length, _bit is 0, _order is Native

## Creates a reader over `data` starting at `offset`.
weave new_reader_at with data as string, offset as int into CarmenReader:
    var o as int is offset
    if o < 0:
        set o is 0
    if o > data.length:
        set o is data.length
    return with _data is data, _offset is o, _end is data.length, _bit is 0, _order is Native

## Creates a reader over `data` that starts in `e`.
weave new_reader_endian with data as string, e as Endianness into CarmenReader:
    var r as CarmenReader is calling new_reader with data
    set r._order is e
    return r

enchanting CarmenReader:
    ## Byte order used by the `read_*` methods.
    weave order into Endianness:
        return self->_order

    ## Selects the byte order for following reads.
    weave with_endian with e as Endianness into void:
        set self->_order is e

    ## Current byte offset.
    weave offset into int:
        return self->_offset

    ## Bytes left before the end of the window.
    weave remaining into int:
        var n as int is self->_end - self->_offset
        if n < 0:
            return 0
        return n

    ## True when the cursor reached the end of the window.
    weave at_end into bool:
        return self->_offset >= self->_end and self->_bit == 0

    ## Moves the cursor to `pos` (clamped to the window).
    weave seek with pos as int into void:
        var p as int is pos
        if p < 0:
            set p is 0
        if p > self->_end:
            set p is self->_end
        set self->_offset is p
        set self->_bit is 0

    ## Skips `n` bytes; returns the number actually skipped.
    weave skip with n as int into int:
        var start as int is self->_offset
        var p as int is self->_offset + n
        if p < 0:
            set p is 0
        if p > self->_end:
            set p is self->_end
        set self->_offset is p
        set self->_bit is 0
        return self->_offset - start

    ## Skips zero bytes until the offset is a multiple of `a`.
    weave align with a as int into void:
        if a <= 1:
            return
        var r as int is self->_offset - ((self->_offset / a) * a)
        if r != 0:
            calling self.skip with (a - r)

    ## Drops a partial bit byte so the next byte read is aligned.
    weave align_bits into void:
        if self->_bit != 0:
            set self->_bit is 0
            if self->_offset < self->_end:
                set self->_offset is self->_offset + 1

    ## True when there are at least `n` bytes left.
    weave has with n as int into bool:
        return (self->_end - self->_offset) >= n

    weave _take_u with n as int into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        if self->_bit != 0:
            return calling err_of with (with Unaligned is with position is self->_bit)
        if self->_offset + n > self->_end:
            return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with n, calling self.remaining)
        var v as u64 is calling _get_u with self->_data, self->_offset, n, self->_order
        set self->_offset is self->_offset + n
        return calling ok_of with v

    ## Reads an unsigned 8-bit integer.
    weave read_u8 into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_u with 1

    ## Reads an unsigned 16-bit integer.
    weave read_u16 into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_u with 2

    ## Reads an unsigned 32-bit integer.
    weave read_u32 into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_u with 4

    ## Reads an unsigned 64-bit integer.
    weave read_u64 into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_u with 8

    weave _take_i with n as int, bits as int into result of i64 to CarmenError:
        var t as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with n
        if not t.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with t.error
        var v as u64 is t.value
        var b as i64 is v to i64
        if bits < 64:
            var sh as int is 64 - bits
            set b is ((v << sh) to i64) >> sh
        return calling ok_of with b

    ## Reads a signed 8-bit integer.
    weave read_i8 into result of i64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_i with 1, 8

    ## Reads a signed 16-bit integer.
    weave read_i16 into result of i64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_i with 2, 16

    ## Reads a signed 32-bit integer.
    weave read_i32 into result of i64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_i with 4, 32

    ## Reads a signed 64-bit integer.
    weave read_i64 into result of i64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self._take_i with 8, 64

    ## Reads a 32-bit float.
    weave read_f32 into result of f64 to CarmenError:
        var t as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with 4
        if not t.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with t.error
        var f as float is calling _f32_from_bits with (t.value to u32)
        return calling ok_of with (f to f64)

    ## Reads a 64-bit float.
    weave read_f64 into result of f64 to CarmenError:
        var t as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with 8
        if not t.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with t.error
        return calling ok_of with (calling _f64_from_bits with t.value)

    ## Reads a half-precision float.
    weave read_f16 into result of f64 to CarmenError:
        var t as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with 2
        if not t.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with t.error
        var f as float is calling _half_to_f32 with (t.value to u16)
        return calling ok_of with (f to f64)

    ## Reads a boolean byte.
    weave read_bool into result of bool to CarmenError:
        var t as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with 1
        if not t.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with t.error
        return calling ok_of with (t.value != 0)

    ## Reads one character.
    weave read_char into result of char to CarmenError:
        var t as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with 1
        if not t.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with t.error
        return calling ok_of with (t.value to char)

    ## Reads `n` bytes as an owned string.
    weave read_bytes with n as int into result of string to CarmenError:
        if n < 0 or not calling self.has with n:
            return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with n, calling self.remaining)
        var out as string is calling _carmen_copy_range with self->_data, self->_offset, n
        set self->_offset is self->_offset + n
        set self->_bit is 0
        return calling ok_of with out

    ## Reads bytes up to the next NUL, which is consumed but not returned.
    weave read_cstr into result of string to CarmenError:
        var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of self->_data
        var k as int is self->_offset
        while k < self->_end:
            if ((bb at k) to int) == 0:
                var out as string is calling _carmen_copy_range with self->_data, self->_offset, k - self->_offset
                set self->_offset is k + 1
                return calling ok_of with out
            set k is k + 1
        return calling err_of with (with MissingTerminator is with position is self->_offset)

    ## Reads a Pascal string of `n` total bytes (length byte + text).
    weave read_pascal with n as int into result of string to CarmenError:
        if n <= 0:
            return calling ok_of with ""
        if not calling self.has with n:
            return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with n, calling self.remaining)
        var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of self->_data
        var l as int is (bb at self->_offset) to int
        if l > n - 1:
            set l is n - 1
        if l < 0:
            set l is 0
        var out as string is calling _carmen_copy_range with self->_data, self->_offset + 1, l
        set self->_offset is self->_offset + n
        return calling ok_of with out

    ## Reads an unsigned LEB128 varint.
    weave read_varint into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        var v as u64 is 0
        var shift as int is 0
        var k as int is 0
        while k < 10:
            var b as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with 1
            if not b.is_ok:
                return b
            var x as u64 is b.value
            if shift >= 64:
                return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with -1, "varint is too long")
            set v is v | ((x & 127) << shift)
            if (x & 128) == 0:
                return calling ok_of with v
            set shift is shift + 7
            set k is k + 1
        return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with -1, "varint is too long")

    ## Reads a ZigZag + LEB128 signed varint.
    weave read_zigzag into result of i64 to CarmenError:
        var r as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self.read_varint
        if not r.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with r.error
        var u as u64 is r.value
        var v as i64 is ((u >> 1) to i64)
        if (u & 1) == 1:
            set v is -v - 1
        return calling ok_of with v

    ## Reads `n` bits (MSB first) as an unsigned integer.
    weave read_bits with n as int into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        if n < 0 or n > 64:
            return calling err_of with (calling _out_of_range with -1, "bit count must be 0..64")
        var acc as u64 is 0
        var k as int is 0
        var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of self->_data
        while k < n:
            if self->_offset >= self->_end:
                return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with 1, 0)
            var cur as int is (bb at self->_offset) to int
            var bit as u64 is (((cur >> (7 - self->_bit)) & 1) to u64)
            set acc is (acc << 1) | bit
            set self->_bit is self->_bit + 1
            if self->_bit == 8:
                set self->_bit is 0
                set self->_offset is self->_offset + 1
            set k is k + 1
        return calling ok_of with acc

    ## Consumes `n` bytes and returns a borrowed slice of them.
    weave view with n as int into result of slice of byte to CarmenError:
        if n < 0 or not calling self.has with n:
            return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with n, calling self.remaining)
        var s as slice of byte is calling _carmen_view with self->_data, self->_offset, n
        set self->_offset is self->_offset + n
        set self->_bit is 0
        return calling ok_of with s

    ## Consumes `n` bytes and returns a reader window over them.
    weave sub with n as int into result of CarmenReader to CarmenError:
        if n < 0 or not calling self.has with n:
            return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with n, calling self.remaining)
        var child as CarmenReader is with _data is self->_data, _offset is self->_offset, _end is self->_offset + n, _bit is 0, _order is self->_order
        set self->_offset is self->_offset + n
        return calling ok_of with child

    ## Requires the next bytes to equal `s`.
    weave expect with s as string into result of void to CarmenError:
        if not calling self.has with s.length:
            return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with s.length, calling self.remaining)
        var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of self->_data
        var sb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
        var k as int is 0
        while k < s.length:
            if (bb at (self->_offset + k)) != (sb at k):
                return calling err_of with (calling _bad with "byte sequence mismatch", self->_offset + k)
            set k is k + 1
        set self->_offset is self->_offset + s.length
        return calling ok_of with 0

    ## Reads the next byte without moving the cursor.
    weave peek_u8 into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self.peek_u64 with 1

    ## Reads the next 16-bit integer without moving the cursor.
    weave peek_u16 into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self.peek_u64 with 2

    ## Reads the next 32-bit integer without moving the cursor.
    weave peek_u32 into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        return calling self.peek_u64 with 4

    ## Reads `n` bytes as a `u64` without moving the cursor.
    weave peek_u64 with n as int into result of u64 to CarmenError:
        var save as int is self->_offset
        var bit as int is self->_bit
        var r as result of u64 to CarmenError is calling self._take_u with n
        set self->_offset is save
        set self->_bit is bit
        return r

    ## Reads the next record described by `fmt`.
    ##
    ## The cursor advances by `calcsize(fmt)`.
    weave read_record with fmt as string into result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError:
        var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
        if not c.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with c.error
        var h as Carmen is c.value
        var need as int is calling h.size
        banish h
        var raw as result of string to CarmenError is calling self.read_bytes with need
        if not raw.is_ok:
            return calling err_of with raw.error
        var blob as string is raw.value
        var r as result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError is calling unpack with fmt, blob
        banish blob
        return r

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Named fields and introspection
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Validates `fmt`, returning the record size or a `CarmenError`.
##
## ## Example
## `var n as int is (calling carmen.validate with ">I4sH").value`
weave validate with fmt as string into result of int to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var n as int is calling h.size
    banish h
    return calling ok_of with n

## Returns a lowercase hexadecimal rendering of the bytes of `s`.
##
## ## Example
## `calling carmen.hex with "AB"` → `"4142"`
weave hex with s as string into string:
    var digits as string is "0123456789abcdef"
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    var bb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
    var i as int is 0
    while i < s.length:
        var v as int is (bb at i) to int
        calling sb.append with (digits at (v >> 4))
        calling sb.append with (digits at (v & 15))
        set i is i + 1
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    return out

weave _field_label with f as CarmenField into string:
    if f.index < 0:
        return calling _carmen_dup with "(pad)"
    if f.name.length == 0:
        return calling _carmen_dup with "(value)"
    return calling _carmen_dup with f.name

## Renders a human-readable layout table for `fmt`.
##
## Columns: index, byte offset, size, alignment, code and field name.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var t as string is (calling carmen.explain with ">I4sH").value
## calling print with t
## banish t
## ```
weave explain with fmt as string into result of string to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    calling sb.append with "idx\toffset\tsize\talign\tcode\tname\n"
    var k as int is 0
    for f in h._fields:
        var code_s as string is chr (f.code to int)
        var label as string is calling _field_label with f
        calling sb.append with "{k}\t{f.offset}\t{f.size}\t{f.alignment}\t{code_s}\t{label}\n"
        banish label
        banish code_s
        set k is k + 1
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    banish h
    return calling ok_of with out

## Renders an annotated hexadecimal dump of `data` according to `fmt`.
##
## One line per field: offset, size, code, name and the field bytes in hex.
weave describe with fmt as string, data as string into result of string to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var need as int is calling h.size
    if data.length < need:
        banish h
        return calling err_of with (calling _truncated with need, data.length)
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    calling sb.append with "offset\tsize\tcode\tname\thex\n"
    for f in h._fields:
        var code_s as string is chr (f.code to int)
        var label as string is calling _field_label with f
        var seg as string is calling _carmen_copy_range with data, f.offset, f.size
        var hx as string is calling hex with seg
        calling sb.append with "{f.offset}\t{f.size}\t{code_s}\t{label}\t{hx}\n"
        banish seg
        banish hx
        banish label
        banish code_s
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    banish h
    return calling ok_of with out

## Unpacks `fmt` into a map keyed by the declared field names.
##
## Every value-producing field must be named; padding fields are ignored.
## Repeated names become `name`, `name#1`, `name#2`, …
##
## ## Errors
## `UnnamedField` when a value field has no name.
##
## ## Memoria
## The map owns the values; release it with `banish`.
weave unpack_named with fmt as string, data as string into result of map of string to CarmenValue to CarmenError:
    var u as result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError is calling unpack with fmt, data
    if not u.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with u.error
    var vals as list of CarmenValue is u.value
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        banish vals
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var m as map of string to CarmenValue is map of string to CarmenValue
    for f in h._fields:
        if f.index >= 0:
            if f.name.length == 0:
                banish vals
                banish h
                return calling err_of with (with UnnamedField is with position is f.offset)
            with m:
                calling .put with f.name, (vals at f.index)
    banish vals
    banish h
    return calling ok_of with m

## Unpacks a buffer holding a whole number of records.
##
## ## Errors
## `BadFormat` when `calcsize(fmt)` is zero or does not divide the buffer.
weave iter_unpack with fmt as string, data as string into result of list of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError:
    var c as result of Carmen to CarmenError is calling seal with fmt
    if not c.is_ok:
        return calling err_of with c.error
    var h as Carmen is c.value
    var step as int is calling h.size
    banish h
    if step <= 0:
        return calling err_of with (with BadFormat is with reason is "record size must be positive", position is 0)
    if data.length % step != 0:
        return calling err_of with (with BadFormat is with reason is "buffer length is not a multiple of the record size", position is 0)
    var out as list of list of CarmenValue is list of list of CarmenValue
    var off as int is 0
    while off < data.length:
        var chunk as string is calling _carmen_copy_range with data, off, step
        var u as result of list of CarmenValue to CarmenError is calling unpack with fmt, chunk
        banish chunk
        if not u.is_ok:
            banish out
            return calling err_of with u.error
        calling out.push with u.value
        set off is off + step
    return calling ok_of with out
